.TH AURA-LAUNCHER 1 "2026-10-29" "aura-launcher 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aura-launcher \- modern GTK4 application launcher for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aura-launcher
[\fB\-\-quit\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aura-launcher
opens a search window for installed applications. Besides launching programs
it evaluates arithmetic expressions, performs web searches, opens URLs and
runs system actions such as locking the screen or shutting down the machine.
.PP
The application runs as a single instance. If a background instance already
exists, invoking the command again simply shows the window.
.PP
Typing filters applications by name, description and keywords. Use the arrow
keys to move, Enter to open the selection and Escape to clear the query or
hide the window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Stop the background instance.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AURA_THEME
Force a colour scheme: \fBdark\fR or \fBlight\fR. By default the desktop
preference is used and followed live.
.TP
.B AURA_LAYER_SHELL
Set to \fB1\fR to use wlr-layer-shell on compositors that support it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/aura-launcher/usage.json
Launch counts used to rank frequently used applications.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B 2^10 + sqrt(144)
Shows the result and copies it to the clipboard on Enter.
.TP
.B g gtk4 tutorial
Searches Google for the given terms.
.TP
.B github.com
Opens the site in the default browser.
